Conclusion
The primary cause of requirement instability is frequent backlog changes by the Product Owner without sufficient refinement or stakeholder alignment. By clearly defining Scrum roles, conducting regular backlog refinement, using structured prioritization techniques such as MoSCoW and Business Value vs. Effort, freezing the Sprint Backlog after Sprint Planning, and implementing actionable improvements during Sprint Retrospectives, the team can reduce requirement churn, improve productivity, and deliver a higher-quality telemedicine application while maintaining stakeholder satisfaction.



